 "post": {
  "title": "Europe wants its own Starlink rival",
  "caption": "Europe wants its own Starlink rival. 🛰️\n\nOn 19 Oct, Deutsche Telekom, Orange, Telefónica and Vodafone signed a letter of intent to explore a joint bid for Europe's mobile satellite spectrum. The idea is direct-to-device: your normal phone connects to satellites where there's no tower. The four would build the ground network and coordination in Europe, while a satellite partner, not chosen yet, would run the constellation. Any mobile operator could buy access on open, equal terms. It's early: a plan to bid, not satellites in orbit.\nSend this to someone who's always out of signal.",
